* vmov_cmp VCTRL step probe body (issue #196). Not a design.
* Deck = design/netlist/lock_detector.spice (committed export) + this body; vmov_cmp alone is
* driven by an ideal VCTRL source that is quiet at 0.600 V and then steps (200 ps edge) by
* +3, -3, -3, +3, +5, -5, -5, +5, +8, -8, -8, +8 mV, one step every 100 ns from 100 ns (the
* sequence returns to 0.600 V; the 10 ns low-pass recovers in 100 ns). STILL (20 fF load as a
* lock-detector input would see) is read over the 60 ns after each step.
Vdd vdd 0 1.2
Vctrl vctrl 0 PWL(0 0.6 100n 0.6000 100.2n 0.6030 200n 0.6030 200.2n 0.6000 300n 0.6000 300.2n 0.5970 400n 0.5970 400.2n 0.6000 500n 0.6000 500.2n 0.6050 600n 0.6050 600.2n 0.6000 700n 0.6000 700.2n 0.5950 800n 0.5950 800.2n 0.6000 900n 0.6000 900.2n 0.6080 1000n 0.6080 1000.2n 0.6000 1100n 0.6000 1100.2n 0.5920 1200n 0.5920 1200.2n 0.6000 1300n 0.6000)
Cl still 0 20f
Bhalf half 0 V = 0.5*v(vdd)
XDUT vctrl still vdd 0 vmov_cmp
